\\\"Both receipts come from the same harness lineage for this question. 226f9762f0b444f69c154b35fe0788f3 is the corrected revision executed twice (the second execution is 7adf927d528b4a74942c03b155aa8557, recorded by repeat); 457abd18451d4fd18ed506ae7f5c5391 is its successor revision, which differs only by adding the shallow case that omits the two client commits after the removal. The resurrection and premature-commit comparisons are identical across all of them, so the earlier receipt remains a valid witness, while the boundary comparison is taken only from the successor where the shallow case exists.\\\")\nch['counterevidence'].append(\\\"The successor receipt also carries the boundary case: with the removal entry still above the replayed prefix (staged commit 5 against entry index 6) the restarted node kept the committed two-server membership and did not resurrect the removed voter (comparison holds at index 9), while the resurrection and premature-commit comparisons scored violated again at indices 1 and 3 with the flag-off control holding at index 7.\\\")\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
